10: +    """The `read-source` command wraps its result as {"payload": {...}} while the other commands
11: +    print their keys flat, so reading `content` or `label` off the top level silently sees None and
12: +    the check fails for the envelope rather than for the file browser. Unwrap when the envelope is
13: +    there and fall through when it is not, so this keeps working whichever shape a caller produces.
14: +    """
15: +    response = run_service('read-source', source_id)
16: +    body = response.get('payload')
17: +    return body if isinstance(body, dict) else response
